  <bioghist id="fa512431946236dd46d2db224ed3037a">
    <head>Biographical / Historical</head>
<p>The Ford Foundation maintained an office in Buenos Aires, Argentina from 1962-1975. Throughout the course of the Buenos Aires office's history, the Foundation's Argentina program focused on supporting projects and initiatives involved with science and technology, education, social science research and training, agricultural development, industrial and trade development, public and private management and administration, and population. </p><p>After the Foundation closed the Buenos Aires office in 1975, its Argentina programming became absorbed under its broader Andean Region and Southern Cone program aims. The Andean Region and Southern Cone office moved from Lima, Peru to Santiago Chile, in 1991.</p>  </bioghist>
  <scopecontent id="e636abae62fc4da6dc74418e55fcea57">
